# ── Derived data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under data/ is reproducible: calibrated/ re-downloads from MAST, and
# drizzled/ + drizzle_files/ regenerate from the scripts. Provenance lives in the
# info/provenance/*.json tracking files (which obsids produced which product), not in the
# bytes. ~185 GB across ~3900 FITS files, so it must never enter git history.
#
# data/stamps is the deliberate exception: the final 12" science stamps (stamp12_*; see
# scripts/stamp_paths.py) and the band's PSF (psf*.fits) are small and worth versioning,
# and the band dirs carry the hand-drawn masks (stamp12_mask.fits) and hand-marked
# positions (stamp12_positions.json), which no script can regenerate. data/mosaics is the
# same deal: small QC grids generated from the stamps by scripts/make_mosaics.py.
#
# Stamps of any OTHER size (stamp20_* etc.) sit in the same band dirs but are NOT
# versioned: they are regenerable from the drizzled mosaics by one runner call
# (run_stamps_all.sh <sample> <size>), and carry no masks of their own since every tool
# defaults to each lens's MODELLING size. Hence the stamp*/!stamp12_* pair below. A lens
# given a smaller modelling size (stamp_size in info/samples/lens_samples.json) needs its
# own !data/stamps/**/stamp<S>_* line here, or its stamps, masks and positions are ignored.
#
# There is ONE stamp per (sample, lens, band, size), and its filename says which reduction
# it is (2026-09-22): stamp12_{sci,noise}.fits is the standard drizzle (what main carries,
# and what the fits use); a variant cut is tagged, stamp12_bcfill_sci.fits (the bcfill
# branch). Masks/positions/PSFs are untagged and shared. The drizzle layer keeps every
# reduction (data/drizzled[_bcfill][_crfill]/, data/drizzle_files*/), all ignored by the
# data/* rule.
data/*
!data/stamps/
!data/mosaics/
data/stamps/**/stamp*
!data/stamps/**/stamp12_*

# ── QC renders of tracked stamps ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# stamp12.png is a plain 3-panel render of the tracked sci/noise stamp, rebuilt by
# make_stamps.py (untracked 2026-10-04, when it had grown to 410 MB of history; the
# stamp*/!stamp12_* pair above already excludes it, since it has no underscore after the
# size). stamp12_positions.png is a QC view OF the tracked stamp12_positions.json, rebuilt
# with no GUI and no re-clicking:
#     uv run python scripts/make_positions.py --sample <sample> --overlays-only
# stamp12_dataset.png is still tracked (the QC view people actually open).
data/stamps/**/stamp12.png
data/stamps/**/*_positions.png

# ── Arc masks: ALL out of git (2026-10-21) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Every stamp12_mask_arcs.{fits,png}, in every sample and band, is held OUT of git (their
# quality is not vouched for; arc masks are optional products anyway). Nothing is deleted:
# the files stay on disk beside the sci they were drawn on, and their provenance stays in
# the tracked info/provenance/lens_arc_masks.json, so make_arc_masks.py still counts them
# done and skips them (--force to redraw). Drop these two lines to track them again.
data/stamps/**/*_mask_arcs.fits
data/stamps/**/*_mask_arcs.png

# ...and neither is the per-size QC provenance for an untracked size, which would
# otherwise be a tracked file describing products nobody else has on disk. The 12"
# info/provenance/lens_stamp_qc.json is tracked, untouched by this pattern.
info/provenance/lens_stamp_qc_*arcsec.json

# ── Large external material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The STScI handbooks and PSF papers the DQ-bit, pixel-scale and read-noise choices
# cite (147 MB of third-party PDFs) live outside the repo tree since 2026-10-25;
# info/instrument_drizzle_ref.md lists each edition with a download link and keeps
# the page-numbered digest.
hst_notebooks/

# ── Superseded notebooks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exploratory / pre-pipeline notebooks. Kept locally but not versioned: they carry
# large embedded output images and re-run churn (execution counts, timestamps) that
# does not belong in history. The live pipeline is scripts/*.py.
scripts/old_notebooks/

# ── Generated output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/

# ── Editor / agent / interpreter state ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Track shared Claude Code config (.claude/settings.json) but keep personal
# per-machine overrides (settings.local.json) out of history.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# ── uv-managed environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pyproject.toml/uv.lock/.python-version are tracked (they define the env, including
# the exact CPython build); the venv itself is machine-local and rebuilt via `uv sync`.
.venv/


# ── diagnostics/ ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-off QC and investigation figures (LACosmic scans, arc-vs-contaminant tests, mask
# proposals). They are regenerable from the scripts and the products in data/, they are
# read once while judging a decision, and they accumulate fast, so they stay out of git.
# The DECISION each figure supported belongs in AGENTS.md / info/*.json, which is where a
# reader should find it -- so do not cite a diagnostics/ path as evidence in a commit
# message or a note without also stating the numbers, because a fresh clone will not have
# the image. Untracked from 2026-09-14; the five previously-committed PNGs remain in git
# history.
diagnostics/
# laptop-only literature notes and analysis scripts (local/literature/, local/scripts/),
# as in the sibling projects
/local/

# ── Private agent notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md imports the tracked AGENTS.md (@AGENTS.md) and adds the maintainer's private
# working notes. Only AGENTS.md is needed to use the repo.
/CLAUDE.md

# ── Exploratory scripts kept out of the public tree ───────────────────────────
# scripts/bolton_investigations/: the standalone prototypes behind the --bcfill decision
# (Bolton-style bilinear reduction, stripe heal, bad-column re-drizzle). Closed
# investigation, superseded by the productionised flag; untracked 2026-10-25, kept on disk.
scripts/bolton_investigations/
